ÒÔš½Ô"…I think some of the recent criticism of the deck may have been a bit unfair.  This deck is presented as a deck to learn vocabulary, and it does this well.  It is not intended to teach grammar.   Many people believe that a good understanding of vocabulary helps with learning grammar at a later time.  It is not a given that grammar comes first.  
What I did with this deck was to use the JLAB deck at the same time.  The JLAB deck's strengths and weaknesses are the opposite of this one.  JLAB covers all of Tae Kim grammar, but the vocabulary are taught slowly.

What follows is a message I wrote some time ago.
Sigh...
Until recently this deck had a nice, supportive community on discord.  However some drama seems to happened in this community, and they have locked out beginners from their discord channel -- the very people who would use this deck and might be interested in seeing where there learning path might go.  I do not understand what happened, but it makes the whole community appear snobby, elitist, and unfriendly.
This is a shame, because this is an excellent deck. It is their discord server and they can run however they want, but I am not sure if I really want to get to know any of the people on the discord server even if I am eventually let in. 
There are many other resources and communities that can support you if you chose to use this deck.
I think it is the best beginner deck around.*¹Hi, thanks for your comment!

I would like to mention that this deck is not affiliated with TMW, the discord server you're mentioning. It is squarely something individuals (and not a server) made. It just so happens that the genesis of the deck happened there because both Tyogin and myself met there, but the place it is hosted is (and always has been) my GitHub page. TMW is not my server and I do not run it. Kaishi is a deck that is used in multiple communities, including Refold for instance. I am not associated with (or run) any specific server. I understand there has been some drama in TMW, but it is unrelated to this deck. 

If you have an issue or would like assistance with the deck, please do not hesitate to use the GitHub issue tracker, which you can find here: https://github.com/donkuri/Kaishi/issues. I have always tried my best to help people that have issues with Kaishi. :)
More generally, this deck, along with all of my other resources can be found here: https://linktr.ee/saegusa.

Many thanks, and I'm sorry for the reception you've gotten in that server.0ñ½
³Ã‡¢Ô"ªI find this one mostly unhelpful and a loss of time as a primer deck, because there is no progression in terms of grammar in the sentences above the first 50 cards or so. It just throws multiple new random grammar points together, seemingly without thinking much about it. If we just want to learn vocab without progression in the sentences, we may as well do immersion sentence mining directly from the beginning. Real immersion would probably be more efficient and it wouldn't really ask more side research and sentence breakdowns compared to this deck
