É²ù°Ï"¾After studying this deck alone, my Japanese listening comprehension has increased to almost 50%. A few of the words are a bit too nuanced, but generally very common and useful words. It is lacking katakana words completely though, so you might miss out on some important words, which you can easily learn later. It also teaches some basic words like numbers or dates later in the deck, which in general is a good thing imo, but it might be too late for your preference. From what I understand, this deck is extracted from the Core 2k/6k decks. So if you think you can learn 6k words, maybe you should try that as well, I haven't tried it yet. But if you have a trip in a few months, give this one a go!
