For those of you having trouble with audio clipping over bluetooth. 
I've had this issue on mac with bluetooth devices, but I suspect it's also a problem on windows and linux.

`ffmpeg -y -f lavfi -i anullsrc=cl=mono:r=16000 -c:a flac -t 12:00:00 perfect_silence.mkv` 

will generate 12 hours of empty audio (only like 12MB) then `mpv ./perfect_silence.mkv`. Now the connection stays open and your audio won't clip.
(or playing music quietly in the background also works).

