Ëøë´Ç"ÀThe choice of vocabulary in this deck is great. Having gone through almost half of the deck (plus some grammar and input), I'm starting to get the gist of most (mundane) Japanese sentences and expressions. The cards mostly have all the information that is needed but not too much. You will also conveniently learn to read a decent number of kanji on the side, especially if you set up the Kanji Popup Dictionary in Anki.

It's not a perfect deck though: Some (and only some) words with multiple/wide meanings have been split into multiple cards without obvious logic which gets confusing during reviews. The images are all over the place and range from ok to actively misleading. I heavily recommend hiding the images from the card layout. The example sentences also range from ok to awful: Some sentences have nothing but unfamiliar words (that often aren't even introduced in the deck), some are so off-kilter that they don't really do much for comprehension. Still, it's better to have the sentences than not, as most will provide at least a bit of context for the use of the word.

Despite the criticisms, this decks is a good learning tool. I do recommend hiding the sentence on the card front by making it a Hint since otherwise you'll just end up remembering the words in that context rather than learning the word itself. It's also not a bad idea to make the sentence translation on the card back a Hint so you can try to figure out the sentence on your own first.
