Âº˜¢·"·Far, far better than Core2k6k! But I do have some minor beef with this deck:
1) Sentence on the front of the card. You can change this by editing the HTML (press E -> Cards)
My issue with having a sentence on the front is that while mnemonics as such are used widely for memorization of things like pi digits they don't work well with words like this, it's an overinvestment of time cause we're built to remember words and not digits of pi, this is simply overkill and slows you down a lot. This can be edited with ease though so not a big deal.
2) Furigana. Furigana is lovely when it's a website that has no other quick way of telling you the reading. It's nice for anki decks if it's just a reading at the bottom like in Core2k, but here particularly as I already know a lot of vocab it simply obstructs me from reading the sentence with just the kanji instead. I'd like an option to have a reading line like in Core2k.

The deck is amazing though!
