- Grumpy*'Kaishi 1.5k - Basic Japanese Vocabulary2% Beginner Japanese Vocabulary Kaishi 8¨Àõ7@´ˆ¦ÕJ³<p><strong><a href="https://linktr.ee/saegusa" rel="noopener noreferrer">Check out the rest of my work as well</a> and <a href="https://donkuri.github.io/learn-japanese/" rel="noopener noreferrer">read the guide</a>!</strong></p>
<p><strong>THIS IS THE ORIGINAL DECK, ANYTHING ELSE NOT DIRECTLY MENTIONED HERE OR ON THE GITHUB WAS DONE WITHOUT MY KNOWLEDGE, INCLUDING ANY AI OR PAID MODIFICATIONS TO THE DECK.</strong></p>
<p>Kaishi 1.5k is a modern Japanese deck in the spirit of Core 2k but with additional features, better coverage optimized through frequency sorting and a modular nature. You can read about the origin of the deck <a href="https://github.com/donkuri/Kaishi?tab=readme-ov-file#the-genesis-of-the-deck" rel="noopener noreferrer">here</a>. You can see the various deck options <a href="https://github.com/donkuri/Kaishi?tab=readme-ov-file#what-options-are-available-for-the-deck" rel="noopener noreferrer">here</a>. <strong>Please use the <a href="https://github.com/donkuri/Kaishi/issues" rel="noopener noreferrer">GitHub page</a> to report issues with the deck</strong>. If you have an issue with the deck, chances are others will as well.</p>
<p>NOW WITH PICTURES! <strong>If you would prefer hiding the sentences in front, please see <a href="https://github.com/donkuri/kaishi?tab=readme-ov-file#i-dont-like-having-sentences-always-on" rel="noopener noreferrer">this option</a>.</strong> In general, there are <em>MANY</em> options presented <a href="https://github.com/donkuri/Kaishi?tab=readme-ov-file#what-options-are-available-for-the-deck" rel="noopener noreferrer">here</a>.</p>
<p><em>If you struggle with kanji, consider doing <a href="https://ankiweb.net/shared/info/1722008986" rel="noopener noreferrer">this related radicals deck</a></em>.</p>
<p><strong>Disclaimer:</strong> This deck is meant to jump-start your immersion. Once you are done with the deck, you are encouraged to start immersing in the language using <a href="https://github.com/themoeway/yomitan" rel="noopener noreferrer">Yomitan</a> and similar tools. For a guide explaining how immersion works, please see <a href="https://donkuri.github.io/learn-japanese/" rel="noopener noreferrer">my guide to learning Japanese</a>.</p>
